# What a fixture.meta means, as both of its readers must read it.
#
# The test program reads fixture metadata with Landin.Testing.Fixtures and
# every Python lane, manifest and check with compiler/tests/fixture_meta.py.
# Each case below is a metadata text, the class directory it sits in, and
# what the readers must make of it: every fault, in order, with the path a
# harness puts before it left out, or for an accepted text the value of each
# named field.  `fixtures/the metadata readers agree` holds the Ada reader to
# this file and scripts/tests/test_fixture_meta.py the Python one, so a
# change to the format that reaches one reader and not the other fails.
#
#   case NAME            begins a case
#   fixture CLASS/NAME   the class directory and the fixture's name
#   | TEXT               one line of the metadata, `|` alone a blank one
#   problem TEXT         a fault the readers report, in order
#   field KEY = VALUE    an accepted fixture's field, as both render it
#   end                  ends the case
#
# A key's field is its value as written.  The others: `status`, the status
# a program must return, and `status@LEVEL` at that level; `traps`, `yes`
# or `no`; `stream`; `profile-count`; `codes-normalized`; `levels@TARGET`,
# the levels TARGET's lane builds at; `source-arguments`, what refine is
# run with, `module-arguments`, its source operands, and
# `program-arguments`, what the compiled program is run with -- each a
# space-separated list, the fixture directory written F/CLASS/NAME.

case a hosted program with every argument key
fixture runtime/reads-input
| class: runtime
| summary: reads a file it is given
| profiles: specialization
| program: main.ldn
| run_args: --level INFO --out build/out.txt
| run_files: input.txt, data/more.txt
| stdin: given.txt
| run_expect: expected.txt
| stream: output
| status: 42
| constructs: 0300, 1810
| targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, linux-rv64, darwin-arm64, cortex-m0
field status = 42
field traps = no
field stream = output
field profile-count = 6
field run_args = --level INFO --out build/out.txt
field run_files = input.txt, data/more.txt
field stdin = given.txt
field module-arguments = F/runtime/reads-input/main.ldn
field source-arguments = F/runtime/reads-input/main.ldn
field program-arguments = --level INFO --out build/out.txt F/runtime/reads-input/input.txt F/runtime/reads-input/data/more.txt
end

case each lane builds only its own family's levels
fixture runtime/every-level
| class: runtime
| summary: a program built at a level of every family
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| status: 7
| levels: x86-64-v3, armv8.1-a, rv64gc_xtheadba, armv7-m
| level_status: rv64gc_xtheadba=8, armv7-m=9
| constructs: 1500
| targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, linux-rv64, darwin-arm64, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, cortex-m0
field levels@linux-x86-64 = x86-64-v3
field levels@freebsd-x86-64 = x86-64-v3
field levels@linux-arm64 = armv8.1-a
field levels@darwin-arm64 = armv8.1-a
field levels@freebsd-arm64 = armv8.1-a
field levels@linux-rv64 = rv64gc_xtheadba
field levels@cortex-m0 = armv7-m
field levels@synthetic-32 =
field status = 7
field status@x86-64-v3 = 7
field status@rv64gc_xtheadba = 8
field status@armv7-m = 9
field profile-count = 4
end

case a rooted negative names its target in args
fixture negative/rooted-target
| class: negative
| summary: refused at one target through its imports
| program: main.ldn
| root: ../../../../..
| args: --target=darwin-arm64
| codes: L0201 ,L0201
| constructs: 0770
| targets: darwin-arm64
field status = 1
field codes-normalized = L0201, L0201
field module-arguments = --root=F/negative/rooted-target/../../../../.. F/negative/rooted-target
field source-arguments = --target=darwin-arm64 --root=F/negative/rooted-target/../../../../.. F/negative/rooted-target
end

case a root of the fixture directory itself
fixture positive/own-root
| class: positive
| summary: the fixture directory is its own root
| program: main.ldn
| root: .
| constructs: 0770
| targets: linux-x86-64
field status = 0
field module-arguments = --root=F/positive/own-root F/positive/own-root
end

case a recorded fixture is run with its args as written
fixture negative/recorded
| class: negative
| summary: a recorded report
| program: program.ldn
| expect: expected.txt
| args: ../tests/fixtures/negative/recorded/program.ldn
| codes: L0302
| status: 1
| constructs: 0910
| targets: linux-x86-64
field source-arguments = ../tests/fixtures/negative/recorded/program.ldn
field module-arguments = F/negative/recorded/program.ldn
end

case a module of several files
fixture positive/two-files
| # a comment, and a blank line, are nothing
|
| class: positive
| summary: one module in two files
| program: main.ldn
| with: other.ldn, more/third.ldn
| constructs: 1840
| targets: linux-x86-64, synthetic-32
field module-arguments = F/positive/two-files/main.ldn F/positive/two-files/other.ldn F/positive/two-files/more/third.ldn
field source-arguments = F/positive/two-files/main.ldn F/positive/two-files/other.ldn F/positive/two-files/more/third.ldn
field with = other.ldn, more/third.ldn
end

case a trapping program has no status
fixture runtime/traps
| class: runtime
| summary: traps
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| traps: yes
| trap_report: main.ldn:4:9: trap: out_of_range
| constructs: 1960
| targets: linux-x86-64
field traps = yes
field trap_report = main.ldn:4:9: trap: out_of_range
field stream = merged
end

case faults in lines
fixture runtime/faulty-lines
| class: runtime
| summary: faulty
| class: runtime
| this line has no colon
| colour: blue
| targets: linux-x86-64, macos-arm64
| profiles: everything
| stream: both
| status: forty
| traps: maybe
| link: dynamic
| constructs: 300
| codes: E0001
problem duplicate key: class
problem line 4 is not `key: value`
problem unknown key: colour
problem unknown target: macos-arm64
problem profiles is not standard or specialization: everything
problem stream is not output or merged: both
problem status is not a number: forty
problem traps is not yes or no: maybe
problem link is not static or libc: dynamic
problem a construct is four digits, and this is not: 300
problem a code is L and four digits: E0001
problem a runtime fixture needs a program to run
end

case files a program is given stay below the fixture
fixture runtime/escaping-files
| class: runtime
| summary: names files outside itself
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| run_files: ../other/input.txt, input.txt, input.txt, /etc/passwd
| stdin: ../../input.txt
| constructs: 0300
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem run_files path is not a file below the fixture directory: ../other/input.txt
problem duplicate run_files path: input.txt
problem run_files path is not a file below the fixture directory: /etc/passwd
problem stdin is not a file below the fixture directory: ../../input.txt
end

case argument keys belong to a program that runs
fixture negative/runs-nothing
| class: negative
| summary: a negative runs no program
| program: main.ldn
| run_args: alpha
| run_files: input.txt
| stdin: input.txt
| run_expect: expected.txt
| profiles: standard
| codes: L0302
| constructs: 0910
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem profiles belong only to a runtime or ABI fixture
problem run_args belong only to a runtime or ABI fixture
problem run_files belong only to a runtime or ABI fixture
problem stdin belongs only to a runtime or ABI fixture
problem run_expect belongs only to a runtime or ABI fixture
end

case a report needs a command and a command a report
fixture end-to-end/half-recorded
| class: end-to-end
| summary: expect alone
| expect: expected.txt
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem expect without args: nothing would produce it
end

case args alone compare nothing
fixture end-to-end/unrecorded
| class: end-to-end
| summary: args alone
| args: --identify
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem args without expect: nothing would be compared
end

case a rooted fixture's args name no module
fixture negative/rooted-module-in-args
| class: negative
| summary: names its module twice
| program: main.ldn
| root: ../../../../..
| args: --target=linux-x86-64 main.ldn --root=elsewhere
| codes: L0201
| constructs: 0770
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem a rooted fixture's args are the options refine takes before the module its root gives, so they name no module: main.ldn
problem a rooted fixture's args are the options refine takes before the module its root gives, so they name no module: --root=elsewhere
end

case levels are some product target's and level_status names them
fixture runtime/bad-levels
| class: runtime
| summary: levels nobody has
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| levels: x86-64-v9, armv8.1-a
| level_status: armv8.1-a=3, rv64gc=4, nonsense
| constructs: 1500
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem level_status entry is not LEVEL=STATUS: nonsense
problem level is no product target's: x86-64-v9
problem level_status names a level levels does not: rv64gc
problem level_status names a level levels does not: nonsense
end

case levels belong to a runtime fixture
fixture positive/levelled
| class: positive
| summary: levels on a positive
| program: main.ldn
| levels: x86-64-v3
| constructs: 1500
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem levels belong to a runtime fixture
end

case C sources belong to their classes
fixture runtime/c-everywhere
| class: runtime
| summary: C where it does not belong
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| with: helper.c
| c-sources: peer.c
| c-args: -lm
| c-shared: plugin.c, other/plugin.c, ../escape.c
| constructs: 0300
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem c-sources belong only to an ABI fixture
problem c-args belong only to an ABI fixture
problem two c-shared sources would build one object: other/plugin.c
problem c-shared path is not a relative .c file: ../escape.c
problem a runtime fixture with c-shared needs link: libc
problem C source belongs in c-sources, never with: helper.c
end

case an ABI fixture needs its C peers
fixture abi/no-peers
| class: abi
| summary: no C
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| constructs: 0300
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem an ABI fixture needs c-sources
end

case a trap has no status, and its report needs a trap
fixture runtime/two-answers
| class: runtime
| summary: traps and returns
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| traps: yes
| status: 3
| constructs: 1960
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem a trapping fixture has no exit status to compare
end

case a trap report without a trap
fixture runtime/report-alone
| class: runtime
| summary: reports a trap it never takes
| profiles: standard
| program: main.ldn
| trap_report: main.ldn:1:1: trap: out_of_range
| constructs: 1960
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem trap_report is the line a trapping program writes, and needs traps: yes
end

case roots, modules and fixes in the wrong places
fixture positive/rooted-with
| class: positive
| summary: rooted and with
| root: ../../../../..
| with: other.ldn
| fixed: main.fixed
| traps: yes
problem missing required key: targets
problem with names the rest of a module and there is no program to be the rest of
problem a rooted positive or negative fixture needs a nonempty program
problem a rooted fixture discovers its module files instead of naming them with `with`
problem fixed belongs only to a negative fixture with a program and codes
problem only a runtime or ABI fixture runs a program that could trap
end

case required keys and a class that disagrees
fixture unit/misfiled
| class: negative
| summary:
| program: main.ldn
problem class negative does not match directory unit
problem summary is empty
problem missing required key: targets
problem a fixture with a program says which constructs it is about
end

case a class no directory has
fixture unit/unknown-class
| class: widget
| summary: an unknown class
| targets: linux-x86-64
problem unknown class: widget
end
